{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms","id":1236678,"title":"On Municipal Charms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-18T22:25:04-07:00","id":1236678,"title":"On Municipal Charms","content":"I've been thinking a bit about Municipal Charms and Alchemical Cities and ....I don't think we actually need a set of really detailed ones. Largely because a game where everyone was playing cities would look more like Civilization or SimCity than Exalted. And, given the niche nature of Alchemicals, I kinda doubt anyone would be able to justify adding enough rules to the game to actually do that setup justice.<br /> <br /> However, the various NPC cities that you have to deal with in Autochthonia do still exist and their capabilities might become important. Like, if you're chasing a criminal and you want to request the city to activate its Infallible Argus Array to search for them, it would be nice to know how that worked. Fortunately, we're likely to get a book that discusses buildings and landscapes with magical powers, up to and including sentience, in the relatively near future. So it seems reasonable to treat Alchemical Cities as particularly high-ranking manses and maybe they'll be able to justify the wordcount for a set of appropriate new Manse powers in the book.<br /> <br /> It seems much more likely than trying to extend the existing Exalted framework past the point it makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T01:25:22-07:00","id":1236692,"title":"","content":"Given the habit of Exalted to to take on the role of King or other rulership positions I kinda feel it is a rather large leap to suggest that people won't be playing the game like Civilization. Further, it has been established that Collosi and Metropoli can deploy normal sized versions of themselves. An alchemical superhero running around a city that responds to their will sounds pretty cool to me.<br /> <br /> Manse rules may work as something like a quick patch, but for people playing the a game at the level where they would be a Metroplois it seems more likely than not that some aspects of Civilization have crept into the game as the Exalted expand their influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","user":"Hark","date":". 07-19-2018, 05:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T02:58:35-07:00","id":1236705,"title":"","content":"The feel I got was that Municipal Charms were both mostly either infrastructure or unique. Or both. But I also got the sense they were more plot devices, so we could get away with just fluff descriptions of some and let the players or STs just wing it from there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T07:07:19-07:00","id":1236755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1236692#post1236692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the habit of Exalted to to take on the role of King or other rulership positions I kinda feel it is a rather large leap to suggest that people won't be playing the game like Civilization. Further, it has been established that Collosi and Metropoli can deploy normal sized versions of themselves. An alchemical superhero running around a city that responds to their will sounds pretty cool to me.<br /> <br /> Manse rules may work as something like a quick patch, but for people playing the a game at the level where they would be a Metroplois it seems more likely than not that some aspects of Civilization have crept into the game as the Exalted expand their influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point. But... I think I was wrong to use Civilization as a comparison. I think Sim City might work better. Because Cities are really more like a cross between the city planner and the chief engineer of a starship. The government tells them what they need and the city makes it happen or tells them &quot;We need more Pylons&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> Which is a very weird perspective to play Exalted from. I'm not gonna say it couldn't be fun, but I think it would take a lot of work and wordcount to make it fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T12:43:38-07:00","id":1236865,"title":"","content":"Solar mayor, sidereal advisors, lunar sheriff, running a metropolis sounds pretty fun to me.<br /> <br /> Synergy works pretty well in exalted, and Alchemicals have a habit of fitting in quite well as the infrastructure when doing teamwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:01:12-07:00","id":1236870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms#post1236678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the various NPC cities that you have to deal with in Autochthonia do still exist and their capabilities might become important. Like, if you're chasing a criminal and you want to request the city to activate its Infallible Argus Array to search for them, it would be nice to know how that worked. Fortunately, we're likely to get a book that discusses buildings and landscapes with magical powers, up to and including sentience, in the relatively near future. So it seems reasonable to treat Alchemical Cities as particularly high-ranking manses and maybe they'll be able to justify the wordcount for a set of appropriate new Manse powers in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Alchemical cities seem to have one or two unique Municipal Charms. I wouldn't be opposed to getting a few of those unique Municipal Charms written out in order to help give a better understanding of the city in question and how it colors the lives of people in that city, as opposed to those living in a city where that unique Charm does not exist. Still, getting an exhaustive list of Municipal Charms is rather pointless because I don't see the &quot;Sim City&quot; playstyle to very popular with most groups (in fact I've never heard of any group running a story with a bunch of city-sized Alchemical PC's).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:52:56-07:00","id":1236886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1236692#post1236692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the habit of Exalted to to take on the role of King or other rulership positions I kinda feel it is a rather large leap to suggest that people won't be playing the game like Civilization. Further, it has been established that <b>Collosi</b> and Metropoli can deploy normal sized versions of themselves. An alchemical superhero running around a city that responds to their will sounds pretty cool to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll point out here that the Devs are on record as saying that becoming a colossi will probably just be another charm. If it works anything like charms in 2E did it'll therefore likely be a removable option. So less 'able to deploy normal sized versions' and more 'I'm in a custom warstrider sized charm but as soon as I take it off I'm still normal&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I should also point out that Alchemicals were specifically an exception to the idea of the exalt always being in charge. The Eight Nations were specifically set up to subvert that and have humans running the show","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T13:57:17-07:00","id":1236889,"title":"","content":"I for one really enjoyed Compass: Autochthonia's way of describing Municipal charms. I loved the idea of entire cities essentially devoted to providing life support and vital functions to the Great Maker while also supporting their citizens and maintaining a safe haven from the dangers of Autochthonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T20:56:29-07:00","id":1237007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms#post1236678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been thinking a bit about Municipal Charms and Alchemical Cities and ....I don't think we actually need a set of really detailed ones. Largely because a game where everyone was playing cities would look more like Civilization</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dammit, why'd you have to mention that game. Now you have me thinking which World Wonders I want to build in my patropoli","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 07-20-2018, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:19:46-07:00","id":1237013,"title":"","content":"btw, security charm:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:38:59-07:00","id":1237017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1236870#post1236870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Alchemical cities seem to have one or two unique Municipal Charms. I wouldn't be opposed to getting a few of those unique Municipal Charms written out in order to help give a better understanding of the city in question and how it colors the lives of people in that city, as opposed to those living in a city where that unique Charm does not exist. Still, getting an exhaustive list of Municipal Charms is rather pointless because I don't see the &quot;Sim City&quot; playstyle to very popular with most groups (in fact I've never heard of any group running a story with a bunch of city-sized Alchemical PC's).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't think it'll work either. But, since there's a large chance that the players in an Autochthonia based game will be inside an NPC city, it's possible that said city might deploy its charms on your behalf in some cases. I suspect the Manse rules, whatever they end up being, could be used to model this with maybe a few parts more added into the final book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T21:41:49-07:00","id":1237019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1237013#post1237013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">btw, security charm:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/iwqN3Ur-wP0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me a little of Castle Heterodyne.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T22:08:12-07:00","id":1237026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1236870#post1236870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Many Alchemical cities seem to have one or two unique Municipal Charms. I wouldn't be opposed to getting a few of those unique Municipal Charms written out in order to help give a better understanding of the city in question and how it colors the lives of people in that city, as opposed to those living in a city where that unique Charm does not exist. Still, getting an exhaustive list of Municipal Charms is rather pointless because I don't see the &quot;Sim City&quot; playstyle to very popular with most groups (in fact I've never heard of any group running a story with a bunch of city-sized Alchemical PC's).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'd prefer it for an ST. PC's will probably rarely need it but it helps for an ST to make a new city or show how a written one works. The mechanics behind a municipal charm would also be helpful. That is how the charm is made, what work goes into charms at that level and how long it takes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T07:46:11-07:00","id":1237141,"title":"","content":"For me the real challenge of city or colossi charms isn't how to balance high essence power, but how to make charms that feel uniquely city.<br /> <br /> Part of the way cool charms are made is if you make people understand how this specific splat can do that thing. City forms may be the final stop for alchemicals, but they operate like completely different splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:10:13-07:00","id":1237150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1237019#post1237019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reminds me a little of Castle Heterodyne.</div> </div> </div> </div>Castle Heterodyne is probably a really good place to go for inspiration on Municipal charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T08:32:40-07:00","id":1237157,"title":"","content":"With the change of how Essence Scaling works in 3E, I strongly expect Colossi to happen at Essence 4-5, then just leave Municiple Alchemicals at Essence 6+. There\u2019s no need to detail Municiple Charms to a playable extent as long as it\u2019s the case that becoming a Metropolis/Patropolis is a choice to ascend and no longer be playing Exalted with that character - hence so many elder Alchemicals clinging to their humanity rather than embracing total Clarity and ascending.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T09:26:55-07:00","id":1237173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1237157#post1237157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the change of how Essence Scaling works in 3E, I strongly expect Colossi to happen at Essence 4-5, then just leave Municiple Alchemicals at Essence 6+. There\u2019s no need to detail Municiple Charms to a playable extent as long as it\u2019s the case that becoming a Metropolis/Patropolis is a choice to ascend and no longer be playing Exalted with that character - hence so many elder Alchemicals clinging to their humanity rather than embracing total Clarity and ascending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being playable is not the same as not being game-relevant though. There are still gonna be plenty of games that take place in Alchemical cities. Municipal charms are useful as setting material more than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T10:18:53-07:00","id":1237186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1236678-on-municipal-charms?p=1237173#post1237173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being playable is not the same as not being game-relevant though. There are still gonna be plenty of games that take place in Alchemical cities. Municipal charms are useful as setting material more than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s why I said \u201cto a playable extent\u201d. A city\u2019s defenses and such getting some mechanics for encounters/challenges makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T15:43:29-07:00","id":1237317,"title":"","content":"Yeah, complete charms for NPCs would be a waste of wordcount. Quick descriptions would go a long way, though. City Alchemicals are a huge part of the autochtonian setting, and the game has spent two editions selling it short. In there, cities are not just cities, but how do you represent that?<br /> <br /> it would be really nice to know what the effect of a municipal vigilance charm when you group of alchemicals are trying to infiltrate. What are the defenses of a frontier alchemical city against an army of hobgoblins? Even detailing a simple rule of thumb for dice bonuses and penalties would be something, even if uninspired.<br /> <br /> Of course, having an idea of how passive an alchemical city-state is would be interesting. What kind of actions a city-alchemical can take(and conversely, what actions they cannot take) , and in what time scale? Do city alchemicals completely give up their sense of time? Developing a completely detached civilization-level game is niche, but knowing how this affects the people on the street is base setting information!<br /> <br /> I'd pay money for an Alchemical Civilization Boardgame, btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T16:46:41-07:00","id":1237336,"title":"","content":"that may resemble more Civ:BE than base Civ<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}